WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.725
Before anything touches a server, the
wave plan runs on the control node alone.

2
00:00:04.725 --> 00:00:09.292
You give it a wave number, and it
writes down exactly what it intends:

3
00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:13.195
every ready server, every
blocked one, the resource group,

4
00:00:13.195 --> 00:00:16.600
region, cloud, both owners
and the exact tag string.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.252
It refuses to go on if there's no wave,
if a region belongs to the other cloud,

6
00:00:21.252 --> 00:00:26.137
if a production server has slipped into
a pilot wave, or if an owner is missing.

7
00:00:26.137 --> 00:00:29.200
Both onboarding playbooks
start with this plan,

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.330
so if the plan stops, no
server is contacted at all.
